 "split": "test",
 "source_instruction": "my high heel size was 6.5",
 "query": "Hey, I swear the walk over to my neighborhood coffee shop this morning was so chaotic I almost turned right back around to go home. A group of tiny, fluffy golden retriever puppies broke free from their walker right at the crosswalk, and they all came barrelling straight at me, tripping over their own too-big paws to lick my ankles and beg for scratches. I ended up kneeling on the sidewalk cooing at them for a full ten minutes, and by the time I got to the shop my usual iced oat milk latte was already sitting on the counter waiting for me because the barista saw the whole puppy pileup through the front window and knew I\u2019d be delayed. I still have a little tuft of golden puppy fur stuck to the cuff of my jeans, honestly, it made my whole day even if I was almost late to sit down and browse for shoes.\nHey, I\u2019m looking through the women\u2019s pumps right now and need a pair with a wedge heel in size 6.5, oh and they have to come with a free matching velvet dust bag too, right? I don\u2019t want to spend more than that amount I always stick to for everyday shoes, you know the one I mean? Wait, make sure they don\u2019t have any weird scuffs on the toe box either, I hate when display pairs have marks. Yeah, just pull up whatever fits those notes for me, thanks!",
